{{!
    @template enrol_apply/profile_missing

    Tells an applicant which profile details they still have to fill in on their own profile
    page, on a site that does not let courses write to profiles.

    Every label is the plain spelling and is rendered through a double stash, so Mustache
    escapes each exactly once, as in enrol_apply/profile_offer beside it.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading string - heading of the block
    * intro string - one line saying the application went in and what is still missing
    * fields array - one entry per missing field, each with its label

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Some details are missing from your profile",
        "intro": "Your application has been submitted. These details are not yet on your profile, and this site does not allow courses to fill them in for you.",
        "fields": [
            {"label": "City/town"},
            {"label": "R&D < Team"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-profile-missing">
    <h3>{{heading}}</h3>
    <p>{{intro}}</p>
    <ul>
        {{#fields}}
            <li>{{label}}</li>
        {{/fields}}
    </ul>
</div>
